{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"InMemoryDestination","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Deliver to it beside the destinations that send events away, then read what arrived: an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in-app event inspector or debug drawer listing what was just tracked, a recent-activity view,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a SwiftUI preview fed sample events, or a test checking what its code tracked."}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let destination = InMemoryDestination(capacity: 500)","let tracker = Tracker()","tracker.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\"))","await tracker.finish()","try await tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: destination).execute()","destination.events(of: SignedUp.self)  \/\/ [SignedUp(plan: \"pro\")]"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It keeps at most "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"capacity"},{"type":"text","text":" records, across batches: once a batch takes it past that, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"oldest records are dropped until the newest "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"capacity"},{"type":"text","text":" remain. A batch some of whose records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"were dropped is kept with the newest of them, so "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/InMemoryDestination\/batches"},{"type":"text","text":" always holds "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/InMemoryDestination\/records"},{"type":"text","text":", in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order